<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 14_pseudo_elements/09: Clearing floats -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Clearing floats</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .clearfix::after { content: ""; display: block; clear: both; }
    .box { background: #fff; border: 2px solid #94a3b8; border-radius: 12px; padding: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .box div { float: left; width: 6rem; height: 5rem; margin: 0.5rem; background: #fda4af; border-radius: 8px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Clearing floats</h1>
    <p class="lead">A ::after clearfix makes a container wrap its floats.</p>
    <div class="box clearfix"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
    <p>The container above stretches around its floated children.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
